Things could get quite unpleasant if a monster pulls a wand of death on
you.  I looked at your list of resistances, and didn't see death
resistance.  That's the major reason for reflection in 3.1 in my eyes,
but there are other benefits.  Even though you might not get harmed by
cold/fire blasts, it can still ruin your potions and scolls, and
electricty could bake your wands.  It's just much nicer not to have to
worry about this kind of thing (also, you can walk into floating eyes
with impunity :).  With eight wishes, a blessed +3 shield of reflection
would have been a good investment, methinks.

While I'm at it, am I the only one who noticed that Amulets of life
saving appear to be more common?  I finally ascended a character in 3.1,
and Ned the Barbarian had used two amulets (damn Archons!) and still had
another six to burn, and only one was from a wish (I didn't start
finding them until after I'd used a wish, natch).  Am I just lucky (my
other really great game, I had found a total of seven in the dungeon,
although it ended in tragedy)?

